Web Plugins is open core. Licensing is per package, not per repository.

MIT
  packages/protocol      @web-plugins/protocol    see packages/protocol/LICENSE
  packages/runtime       @web-plugins/runtime     see packages/runtime/LICENSE
  packages/widget-kit    @web-plugins/widget-kit  see packages/widget-kit/LICENSE
  apps/views             @web-plugins/views       see apps/views/LICENSE
  examples/hello-widget                           see examples/hello-widget/LICENSE

  Everything that ships to a visitor's browser, plus the shared config and RPC
  contracts, is MIT. Embed it in commercial products without obligation.

AGPL-3.0-only
  apps/server            @web-plugins/server      see apps/server/LICENSE

  The control plane (API, admin panel, database) is AGPL-3.0-only. Self-host it
  freely. If you run a modified version as a network service, section 13
  requires you to offer that source to its users. For a commercial license
  without that obligation, contact the copyright holder.

